Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
## Bezier curves
Here is more compliced example on generating many lines, that all depends on the same symbols:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Bezier curves
Here is more compliced example on generating many lines, that all depends on the same symbols:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  InitGroup: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
autoLine[t_, p1_, p2_, p3_] := 
 Line[
   With[{pc = p2, pi = p1, pf = p3}, 
     {pi + t (pc - pi), pc + t (pf - pc)}
   ] // Offload
 ]

SetAttributes[autoLine, HoldRest]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Now we can plot it with draggable points

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Now we can plot it with draggable points

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  InitGroup: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
curve[p1_, p2_, p3_] := LeakyModule[{pi = p1, pc = p2, pf = p3},
  {
    Blue, Table[autoLine[t, pi, pc, pf], {t, 0, 1, 0.1}],
    PointSize[0.06], Red, 

    EventHandler[Point[pi], {"drag" -> Function[xy, pi = xy]}],
    EventHandler[Point[pc], {"drag" -> Function[xy, pc = xy]}],
    EventHandler[Point[pf], {"drag" -> Function[xy, pf = xy]}]
  }
]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
__Draw__

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
__Draw__

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
curve[{0.2,0.2}, {0.3,0.5}, {0.6,0.1}] // Graphics

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Note, that actual calculation of the intermediate blue line happens on frontend's side, i.e. in the browser. Kernel is only updating the positions of three points `p1`, `p2`, `p3`.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Note, that actual calculation of the intermediate blue line happens on frontend's side, i.e. in the browser. Kernel is only updating the positions of three points `p1`, `p2`, `p3`.

